---
import CartesianGraph from "./primitives/cartesian-graph.astro";
---

<CartesianGraph
  captionSlot
  size="lg"
  title="Convex Isoquant"
  desc="A convex isoquant with tangent lines that become flatter as labour replaces capital, illustrating diminishing marginal rate of technical substitution."
  y={{ label: "Capital (K)", domain: [0, 10] }}
  x={{ label: "Labour (L)", domain: [0, 10] }}
  curves={[
    {
      equation: (labour) =>
        -0.0307 * labour ** 3 + 0.6112 * labour ** 2 - 4.4526 * labour + 13.323,
      derivative: (labour) => -0.0921 * labour ** 2 + 1.2224 * labour - 4.4526,
      domain: [1.32, 8.87],
      tone: "s5",
      tangents: [
        { at: 2.45, domain: [1.5, 3.4], tone: "ink", dashed: true },
        { at: 6.23, domain: [5.2, 7.3], tone: "ink", dashed: true },
      ],
    },
  ]}
  points={[
    { x: 2.45, y: 5.63, tone: "ink" },
    { x: 6.23, y: 1.88, tone: "ink" },
  ]}
  labels={[
    { text: "A", x: 2.45, y: 5.63, tone: "ink", dx: -20, dy: -10, weight: 700 },
    { text: "B", x: 6.23, y: 1.88, tone: "ink", dx: 10, dy: -5, weight: 700 },
    { text: "Q₁", x: 5.19, y: 4.06, tone: "s5", size: 15, weight: 700 },
    { text: "Steeper", x: 0.94, y: 7.19, tone: "ink" },
    { text: "Flatter", x: 7.08, y: 1.41, tone: "ink" },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    A convex isoquant reflects diminishing MRTS: as more labour replaces
    capital, the amount of capital that can be given up for an additional unit
    of labour decreases.
  </Fragment>
</CartesianGraph>
